

# Repro development environment cache
.repro/

# The pre-commit config is GENERATED and must not be tracked -- it is a symlink
# to an absolute /nix/store path valid only on the machine that generated it.
# git-hooks.nix writes it from the devShell shellHook on every entry.
#
# It WAS tracked here (git mode 120000), which is how a dangling symlink came to
# be checked in: `pre-commit` answers "InvalidConfigError:
# .pre-commit-config.yaml is not a file" for it off its build host, and on
# Windows it is a text file naming a path that does not exist.
#
# REMOVE THIS LINE if this repo ever adopts the portable committed form from
# repo-requirements.md section 4.1 -- a real committed config must be tracked,
# and an ignore line left behind is what made that form impossible in a sibling
# repo.
.pre-commit-config.yaml
